1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,812
This tutorial posts a tenancy contract,
which writes

2
00:00:02,812 --> 00:00:05,273
its accounting entries and makes it
active.

3
00:00:05,273 --> 00:00:07,382
As a Company Admin, open Leasing.

4
00:00:07,382 --> 00:00:09,843
The pinned view Contracts to post lists

5
00:00:09,843 --> 00:00:12,304
the contracts still waiting for this step.

6
00:00:12,304 --> 00:00:14,413
Open unit M-1501, Sara Mansour's contract.

7
00:00:14,413 --> 00:00:17,576
Its status is Draft, so nothing has
reached the

8
00:00:17,576 --> 00:00:20,389
ledger yet, and it can still be edited.

9
00:00:20,389 --> 00:00:24,256
It has two charge lines, each credited to
its own account.

10
00:00:24,256 --> 00:00:27,419
The security deposit is held for the
tenant, not

11
00:00:27,419 --> 00:00:30,583
income, so it goes to the Security Deposit
account.

12
00:00:30,583 --> 00:00:33,044
The rent goes to Advance Rent, and

13
00:00:33,044 --> 00:00:35,153
it is earned over the term.

14
00:00:35,153 --> 00:00:36,559
Open the Cheques tab.

15
00:00:36,559 --> 00:00:39,371
The grid holds the five post-dated cheques
Sara

16
00:00:39,371 --> 00:00:42,184
handed over: the deposit, and four rent
instalments.

17
00:00:42,184 --> 00:00:44,996
Their total must equal the contract value
of

18
00:00:44,996 --> 00:00:47,808
140,000, and the grid confirms that it
does.

19
00:00:47,808 --> 00:00:51,323
If it did not, the contract could not be
posted.

20
00:00:51,323 --> 00:00:52,378
Select Post Contract.

21
00:00:52,378 --> 00:00:54,839
Review before posting runs every check a

22
00:00:54,839 --> 00:00:56,948
post would run, and writes nothing.

23
00:00:56,948 --> 00:01:00,815
It shows the contract value, the VAT, and
the cheque total,

24
00:01:00,815 --> 00:01:04,681
and it lists what posting will write: one
tenancy contract journal,

25
00:01:04,681 --> 00:01:08,548
and one post-dated cheque journal for each
of the five cheques.

26
00:01:08,548 --> 00:01:11,712
It reports Ready to post, so select Post
Contract.

27
00:01:11,712 --> 00:01:14,173
The contract is now Active, and the

28
00:01:14,173 --> 00:01:16,282
banner names the journal it wrote.

29
00:01:16,282 --> 00:01:20,149
In the Cheques tab, open Journal Vouchers
to see all six.

30
00:01:20,149 --> 00:01:21,555
Then open Revenue recognition.

31
00:01:21,555 --> 00:01:25,070
The rent is already planned across the
term, one row

32
00:01:25,070 --> 00:01:28,234
per month, each using its real number of
days.

33
00:01:28,234 --> 00:01:32,101
Every row is Planned, and the total
matches the contract rent.

34
00:01:32,101 --> 00:01:34,561
Once posted, a contract is not edited.

35
00:01:34,561 --> 00:01:38,077
Changes are made with actions such as
Amend Lines, Extend

36
00:01:38,077 --> 00:01:41,592
Contract, or Add charge, and each writes
its own entries.
